<title>JAPAN: Japan likely to offer 6-yr JGB on Thursday-sources.</title>
<headline>Japan likely to offer 6-yr JGB on Thursday-sources.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Ministry of Finance (MOF) is likely to offer six-year government bonds through a price-competitive auction next Thursday, market sources said on Friday.</p>
<p>MOF is also likely to offer Treasury bills (T-bills) sometime next week, the sources said.</p>
<p>The T-bill offer is likely to be a roll-over of 1.4 trillion yen worth of six-month T-bills maturing on May 12, bond traders said.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-9780</p>
</text>
